    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's hard to keep separating the art from the actual feeling though. it's like the poem is telling me that the only way to truly capture that \"beauty of the collapse\" is to actually be part of it. i look at my work and then i look at my life, and it feels like the art is calling me to stop being a spectator and actually become the tragedy. like, if i want the work to be perfect, i shouldn't just write about the end, i should embrace it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
